    "updated_at": "2023-03-10T12:37:07Z",
    "body": "I forgot to speak about the `asset` element (you can see it on the document element head).\r\nThis is part of this proposal. This is an element to group some ressource declaration.\r\n\r\n**Retro compatibility**\r\n\r\nActually it will be considered as an unknownHTMLElement, but it already works on chromium and firefox.\r\n\r\nWarning : Puting favicon on it does not work on chromium, but works on firefox. \r\ntitle, css and js works in both.\r\n\r\nWe need more deep tests for each browsers and each possible ressources declaration relatives elements",
